{"name":"Black Metal","hex":"#060606","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black metal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Iron, or similar metals worked by a blacksmith","A subgenre of heavy metal music employing fast tempos, shrieked vocals, highly distorted guitars, double-kick drumming, raw recording and unconventional song structure, often emphasizing antireligious and misanthropic themes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_metal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black metal","blocks":[{"text":"Black metal is an extreme subgenre of heavy metal music. Common traits include fast tempos, a shrieking vocal style, heavily distorted guitars played with tremolo picking, raw (lo-fi) recording, unconventional song structures, and an emphasis on atmosphere. Artists often appear in corpse paint and adopt pseudonyms."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_metal","wikidata":"Q132438"},{"title":"Black Metal (Venom album)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Metal is the second studio album by English heavy metal band Venom, released on 1 November 1982 through Neat Records. Released during the new wave of British heavy metal, the album is considered to be a major influence on the speed metal, thrash metal, death metal and black metal scenes that emerged in the 1980s and early 1990s."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/67/Venomblackmetal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Metal_(Venom_album)","wikidata":"Q804229"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal","wikidata":"Q11426"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Gorgoroth_I.jpg/500px-Gorgoroth_I.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Gorgoroth_I.jpg/1280px-Gorgoroth_I.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Gorgoroth_I.jpg/500px-Gorgoroth_I.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Members of Gorgoroth wearing typical black metal gear such as corpse paint, spikes and bullet belts. The band was formed by guitarist Infernus to express his Satanist beliefs.[19]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGorgoroth_I.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Hindvir_Gaulhammer_Fest_111008_01_C.jpg/500px-Hindvir_Gaulhammer_Fest_111008_01_C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Hindvir_Gaulhammer_Fest_111008_01_C.jpg/1280px-Hindvir_Gaulhammer_Fest_111008_01_C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Hindvir_Gaulhammer_Fest_111008_01_C.jpg/500px-Hindvir_Gaulhammer_Fest_111008_01_C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A common black metal convention is the use of corpse paint, black-and-white make-up intended to make the wearer look inhuman, corpse-like, or demonic. Shown here: Taalroth of French pagan band Hindvir.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHindvir_Gaulhammer_Fest_111008_01_C.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Venom_live_at_hellfest.jpg/500px-Venom_live_at_hellfest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Venom_live_at_hellfest.jpg/1280px-Venom_live_at_hellfest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Venom_live_at_hellfest.jpg/500px-Venom_live_at_hellfest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Venom's second album, Black Metal, inspired the name of the genre.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVenom_live_at_hellfest.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Immortal_Getaway_Rock_Festival.jpg/500px-Immortal_Getaway_Rock_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Immortal_Getaway_Rock_Festival.jpg/500px-Immortal_Getaway_Rock_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Norwegian band Im